'''''Weissia''''' is a genus of [[mosses]], belonging to the family [[Pottiaceae]].<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=Weissia xylopiae Bat. & M.P.Herrera |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/5493569 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=15 January 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

The genus was described in 1801 by [[Johann Hedwig]] and the latest additions to the genus were in 1995 when ''[[Weissia ovatifolia]]'' and ''[[Weissia patula]]'' were added. As of July 2021, the genus contains 91 species.<ref Name="COL">{{Catalogue of Life 
     |id=87LBW
     |title=''Weissia''
     |option=
     |access-date=24 April 2021
}}</ref>

Selected species:
* ''[[Weissia crispula]]''
* ''[[Weissia controversa]]''
* ''[[Weissia brachycarpa]]''
* ''[[Weissia microstoma]]''
* ''[[Weissia squarrosa]]''
* ''[[Weissia xylopiae]]'' {{small|Bat. & M.P.Herrera}}<ref name="GBIF" />

